  "notes": "Government-service style (GOV.UK/USWDS-like) plan chooser personalized to a family's case: rows are the household's own doctors, child's inhaler and pharmacy, each tagged with whose need it is (Angela/Mateo pills). Status uses triple-coded encoding (filled circle icon + colored bold text + tinted cell background) for covered / covered-with-a-catch / not covered, with a legend at table bottom and plain-language consequence text in cells ('Mateo would need a different pulmonologist'). Default-assignment plan is flagged with an amber 'Assigned if you don’t choose' pill and an amber deadline banner; the deadline cell in the case strip is tinted amber. Selecting a plan's radio fills its button teal and tints the whole column light blue with teal borders; the sticky bottom 'Your selection' bar then shows the choice and a one-line consequence and enables 'Review and submit'. No sticky bottom action bar entry exists in the codebook (coded under wizard). Note: in the full-page capture the sticky bar overlays the Valley Children's Clinic row (~y 820–900)."
